MedBullets — NOT REDISTRIBUTED
==============================

The MedBullets items are part of the benchmark suite as analysed in the paper,
but the data file is deliberately NOT included in this repository.

Why
---
No licence could be established for this dataset. The Hugging Face mirror we
drew from declares none, and the originating repository contains no LICENSE file
(verified 2026-08-20: github.com/HanjieChen/ChallengeClinicalQA/blob/main/LICENSE
returns HTTP 404). The underlying questions derive from a commercial medical
question bank, so the absence of a licence appears deliberate rather than an
oversight: the authors were not in a position to grant redistribution rights.

Material published without a licence is "all rights reserved" by default. Rather
than redistribute 308 items with no permission behind them, we omit the file and
point to the source instead.

Where to get it
---------------
Upstream dataset:        https://huggingface.co/datasets/LangAGI-Lab/medbullets_op5
Originating repository:  https://github.com/HanjieChen/ChallengeClinicalQA

Obtain the data from upstream directly, on whatever terms the authors provide.

How to reconstruct our subset
-----------------------------
item_ids.csv in this directory lists the 308 item ids that make up the pre_qc
release of this benchmark. Identifiers are references, not content, so they are
included here. To rebuild the file:

  1. Download medbullets from the upstream source above.
  2. Keep the five-option subset.
  3. Filter to the ids in item_ids.csv.
  4. Convert to the Prj-BENCH schema (id / question / options / target / kind)
     and save as medbullets.json in this directory.

The harness will then pick it up automatically — it globs for *.json — and the
pre_qc release will return to its full item count. With the file absent, the
harness simply runs the other 23 benchmarks.

Citation
--------
Chen, H., Fang, Z., Singla, Y. & Dredze, M. Benchmarking Large Language Models
on Answering and Explaining Challenging Medical Questions. Proc. NAACL (2025).


Language Models on Answering and Explaining Challenging Medical Questions.
Proceedings of NAACL 2025.

Modifications we applied (for reproduction)
-------------------------------------------
  - Converted to the common Prj-BENCH multiple-choice JSON schema
    (id / question / options / target / kind).
  - Five-option subset.
  - No quality-control exclusions applied (this is the pre-QC release).
